WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.386
Hi! The water you drank today might once have been part of a cloud, or a drop in the sea! Let's learn about the water cycle.

2
00:00:10.536 --> 00:00:17.682
The water on Earth doesn't get used up, because it keeps going round in a cycle. Let's go step by step.

3
00:00:17.832 --> 00:00:28.410
Step one: the Sun heats water in the seas, rivers and lakes. The water evaporates into water vapour and rises. Plants give off water vapour too.

4
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:39.474
Step two: high up, the air is cooler. The water vapour loses heat and condenses into tiny water droplets. Lots of droplets together form clouds.

5
00:00:39.624 --> 00:00:47.034
Step three: the tiny droplets join into bigger drops. When they become too heavy, they fall as rain.

6
00:00:47.184 --> 00:00:58.266
Step four: rainwater flows into rivers and lakes and back to the sea. Some soaks into the ground. Then the cycle starts all over again.

7
00:00:58.416 --> 00:01:01.482
Let's draw the water cycle as a loop.

8
00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:05.298
Water in the sea evaporates into water vapour.

9
00:01:05.448 --> 00:01:09.402
The water vapour condenses high up to form clouds.

10
00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:13.266
The droplets in the clouds grow and fall as rain.

11
00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:19.002
The rain flows back to the sea, and the cycle goes on and on.

12
00:01:19.152 --> 00:01:28.314
Sea water is salty, so we can't drink it. But when water evaporates, the salt stays behind in the sea, and the rain that falls is fresh water.

13
00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:36.114
So the water cycle keeps refilling rivers, lakes and the soil with fresh water for plants, animals and people.

14
00:01:36.264 --> 00:01:44.394
Water just moves between different places and states. That's why we must take good care of clean water.

15
00:01:44.544 --> 00:01:50.898
Watch out! Many pupils say clouds are made of water vapour. That's not right!

16
00:01:51.048 --> 00:01:57.978
Water vapour is invisible. We can see clouds because they are made of many tiny water droplets.

17
00:01:58.128 --> 00:02:04.938
Water vapour condenses high up into tiny droplets, and that's how clouds form.

18
00:02:05.088 --> 00:02:16.746
Your turn! High up, water vapour turns into tiny droplets. What is this process called? Pause and think.

19
00:02:16.896 --> 00:02:24.402
The answer is condensation. The water vapour loses heat. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:24.552 --> 00:02:33.930
Another one! Why does water vapour condense when it rises high up? Pause and think.

21
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:43.602
Because it is cooler high up. The water vapour loses heat and condenses into tiny droplets. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:43.752 --> 00:02:53.106
Last one! Sea water is salty, so why is rain fresh water? Pause and think.

23
00:02:53.256 --> 00:03:02.970
Because when water evaporates, only the water turns into vapour. The salt stays behind in the sea. Did you get it right?

24
00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:17.106
Remember: the Sun makes water evaporate, the vapour condenses into clouds high up, the droplets grow and fall as rain, and the water flows back to the sea. The water cycle keeps giving us fresh water.

25
00:03:17.256 --> 00:03:22.530
Next time it rains, think about where that water came from!

